==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|obez}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|obez}}, {{m|goh|obaz||fruit}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*ubatją||fruit, produce, increase}}, from a compound whose first element represents {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*obʰi-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ebʰi-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*bʰi-||on, toward, from, by}}, and whose second element is {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*at}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ēta-||edibles, food}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*etaną||to eat}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁ed-||to eat}}. Cognate with {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|ovest||mast}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{m|gml|ōvet}}, {{m|gml|āvet}}, {{m|gml|ōft||fruit}}, {{etyl|nds|-}} {{m|nds-de|Aaft||fruits}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|ooft||fruits}}. More at {{l|en|ovest}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=de|/oːpst/}}
* {{audio|De-Obst.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Obstes|gen2=Obsts|-}}

# Edible plant parts, other than nuts, which are mainly eaten with sweet dishes, primarily [[fruit]] and [[berry|berries]]. Edible parts of plants which do not count as [[vegetables]].
#: {{ux|de|Heute esse ich nur '''Obst'''.|t=Today I only eat '''fruit'''.|inline=1}}

